# ORCLHUNT: the energizer, which turns the whole board inside out (M16.5).
#
# An energizer changes three separate things, and this scenario takes all three
# against the real ZZT.EXE:
#
#   1. CalcDirectionSeek negates its own answer while World.Info.EnergizerTicks
#      is positive, so every creature that seeks RUNS AWAY. The lion in row 13
#      is charging the player when the energizer is picked up and spends the
#      rest of its life backing into the solid at 13,13.
#   2. BoardAttack pays the player instead of hurting them. Walking into the
#      cornered lion adds its ScoreValue and does NOT call DamageStat on the
#      player (GAME.PAS:1224, first branch); being attacked BY a creature while
#      energized adds the attacker's ScoreValue instead of costing 10 health
#      (the same routine's second branch). One energizer each, so both branches
#      are read off the sidebar separately.
#   3. The player's own square stops being 0x1F: ElementPlayerTick flashes it
#      off CurrentTick — `0x0F` on odd ticks and `(CurrentTick mod 7 + 1) * 16 +
#      0x0F` on even ones — and toggles the E_PLAYER character between 1 and 2.
#      M16.3 could not compare an energized checkpoint at all, because the
#      adapter pinned CurrentTick to 0 and vanilla picks it with Random(100).
#      The M16.4 phase solver removed that restriction: `phase` here means the
#      flash colour and character are compared like any other cell, and they are
#      what makes this scenario's phase pin as tight as it is.
#
# A bear ignores all of this, and that is deliberate: ElementBearTick never calls
# CalcDirectionSeek — it steps by Signum straight off the player's position — so
# an energized player is still charged by bears. The duplicator at 30,13 (source
# direction east, reading the bear at 31,13, writing to 29,13) is here to supply
# them: a duplicated creature carries the SOURCE stat's P1/P2/Cycle, so each copy
# hunts exactly like its original. Copies walk west down the lane and stop
# against the second energizer at 25,13, which is not walkable — so the moment
# the player picks that energizer up, the bear behind it is adjacent and attacks
# into branch 2 above.
#
# Health and score are the compared counters, and health never moves at all:
# 100 throughout, with the score going 0 -> 1 (the cornered lion, eaten) ->
# 2 (a bear charging into a player who has just picked up the second energizer,
# which pays instead of biting) -> 3 (that bear's replacement, walked into).
# The energizer runs out in between — its warning melody at ten ticks left is in
# the compared sound stream — and the checkpoint after it expires is the one
# that proves the flash colour went back to plain 0x1F.
world ORCLHUNT
seed 0
phase
boot 240
capture title
play
# Hunt Hub: unpause and cross the east border opening at 60,13.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture arrive
# Two steps east onto the energizer; the charging lion turns and runs.
move right
move right
capture energized
settle 16
capture lion-fleeing
# Chase it into the corner at 12,13 and eat it.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture cornered
move right
capture lion-eaten
# Stand still until the energizer runs out.
settle 60
capture energizer-spent
# Around the backstop by row 12 and east down the lane to the second energizer.
move up
move right
move right
move right
move down
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture approach
move right
capture bear-bites-back
move right
capture bear-eaten
settle 40
capture duplicated
